  "premise_review": [
    "IsCriticalLineRealPart x is exactly x = Core.spectralPivot. CenteredWithZeroVariance x is exactly Harmonic.CenteredAroundHalf 0 x. The captured AnalyticPivot defines this as absolute deviation from analyticEquilibrium bounded by zero, with analyticEquilibrium defined as Core.spectralPivot.",
    "The first proof obtains absolute-value zero via le_antisymm and abs_nonneg, derives the subtraction equality, unfolds the equilibrium and uses the exact original linarith. The converse keeps x/h, rewriting and simp. The equivalence uses the exact original ordered pair of implication proofs.",
    "No statistical random variable or variance is defined. No hypothesis asserts that an actual L-function zero satisfies either predicate; these are scalar normalization facts only.",
    "The captured root DualPivot context defines spectralPivot as one half, but its root hint is not activated as Core/DualPivot. Original imports and unresolved historical lookup identities remain unchanged. The exact AnalyticPivot path context is preserved without import replay."
  ],
